Hi Andrada,

The user maintains the belief that without physical metrological devices, they cannot be charged more, a point they have emphasized repeatedly”. Also, the user says that “_I remind you that the law applicable to ride-sharing applications stipulates that these applications (_*_in the absence of approved and metrologically verified means of measurement_*_) must offer a price that the customer must accept or not._ *_The price can only be changed after measurements with special metrologically verified devices. I have not seen such a thing in the car in question._*”

I remember we had the discussion before, if he continues to address this although an explanation was already provided to him, then we shall ignore. In case the below was not sent to him:

Bolt app is providing a digital platform where transport operators offer *alternative transport services* to passengers. Both the digital platform operator (Bolt) and the transport operators provide services in accordance with *GEO 49/2019* on *alternative transport activities* with passenger car and driver. In relation to alternative transport services, *GEO 49/2019 is the only law that applies*, other transport laws do not apply to the services in question. 

Thus, according to GEO 49/2019, the digital platform (Bolt) must:

* *propose, display and record the route taken, using location technologies* in accordance with the European legislation;
* provide data on the fare for the route established before the passenger accepts the ride;
* monitors all rides, continuously, through a tracking system;
* provides the passenger with the option of settling the price of the trip based on an electronic payment instrument with remote access or in cash.

Transport operators that have authorisations to perform alternative transport services *do not have the obligation to use a taximeter* or any other such devices, the digital platform is monitoring the rides through a *digital tracking system*. 

Regarding the price, Bolt app calculates the price in advance, taking into consideration the route, the traffic, the demand and supply. Bolt app is informing the passengers before the trip takes place that the price might change due to unexpected events or if the transport operator takes another route. As well, Bolt app displays the following information before the ride starts:
- Estimated price, minimum price, starting price, price per km, price per minute;
- Waiting time costs;
- Cancellation fee. 

The passenger is fully informed how the price is calculated; all rides are monitored through a tracking system and the route is recorded using location technologies, which allows Bolt app to calculate the final price in case changes were registered on the route.

