{quote}Health check should be performed after code in Bootstrap has finished executing (the service restores its' state from Kafka topics){quote}

At this point service is already registered in the service discovery and receives traffic. Is that expected?

{quote}the service restores its' state from Kafka topics{quote}

Could you please elaborate, on what exactly is restored and how is related to the service-level health check? And can you please give more real-world examples of such health checks (e.g. what exactly do you want to execute in the health check?). 



Right now, you have the option to execute such a check as a part of the bootstrap (before the service is registered in the service discovery). In case this check fails, you can see errors in Kibana and Builder health check will fail.

Another option is to cover your service with alerts that monitor business metrics that you need. This way during the deployment you can check alerts and decide what to do next.

