I have reviewed the final versions of the drafts you shared. Everything seems ok and I can see that they accepted all our suggestions except one. They have amended article 2 of the General Terms to exclude indirect damages. Can you please try to agree with them to accept our originally proposed wording? This is our new contractual standard to carve out confidentiality and data protection obligations from liability limitation. You can provide them the following explanation:

{quote}Article 2 of the General Terms - Article 5 of the General Terms stipulates obligations related to confidentiality and data protection. To the extent it concerns breaches of confidentiality and data protection obligations, indirect damages are perhaps the only type of damages one might expect to incur. Upon breach of confidentiality or data protection obligations no assets are damaged or destroyed and third party claims are unlikely - instead, it is the company’s position towards its competitors and reputation towards its customers and partners which would be damaged - and these would manifest primarily through decreased sales, lost business opportunities, lost market share, decreased valuation and the like – all indirect damages. Therefore, our standard position is to extend liability for confidentiality and data protections breaches to indirect damages.{quote}
